`dafny audit` no longer reports the reveal lemma that Dafny generates for an `opaque const` as a ghost declaration that has no body and has an ensures clause, and under `--modular-termination`, `dafny build --target:lib` no longer refuses it as an unchecked premise, so a library may declare an `opaque const`, in a concrete module or in a module that refines one. The lemma states the constant's definition, which holds without it. A bodyless lemma with a postcondition that the user writes is still reported and refused (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/371).
